# ⚠ THIS FILE, NOT ONLY netlify.toml. Netlify reads netlify.toml from the REPOSITORY ROOT (or a
# configured base directory), and this project's copy lives in web-demo/ — so its headers were
# never applied to the deployed site. Measured: `curl -I https://vernacula.netlify.app/` returned
# no Cross-Origin-* headers at all, the page was therefore not cross-origin isolated,
# SharedArrayBuffer was withheld, and WASM inference silently fell back to ONE thread — roughly 6x
# slower than the 8 the machine can run.
#
# A `_headers` file is deployed as part of the publish directory itself, so it applies whatever the
# base directory is set to and however the deploy was made. netlify.toml is kept in step for local
# `netlify dev`, but this is the one that reaches production.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# Hand-editable and regenerated together; a stale voices.jsonc against a fresh voice-codes.json
# lands as `voice "x" has no codes`.
/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

# Content-addressed by build, safe to cache hard.
/vphon-data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
